-- title:
--   A variable change inducing the identity on Proj is trivial
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $T$ whose discriminant $\Delta_W$ is a unit, and let $C=(u,r,s,t)$ be a Weierstrass variable change over $T$ fixing $W$, i.e. $C\bullet W=W$. Write $\mathrm{projModelGradingCR}$ for the grading of $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,3)\,T$ modulo the ideal generated by the homogeneous Weierstrass cubic, given by the images of the homogeneous submodules under the quotient map, and $\mathrm{projModelCR}$ for the associated $\mathrm{Proj}$. Let $\varphi$ be a graded ring homomorphism from the grading attached to $W.\mathrm{toProjective}$ to the one attached to $(C\bullet W).\mathrm{toProjective}$ such that the irrelevant ideal of the target is contained in the ideal generated by the image under $\varphi$ of the irrelevant ideal of the source, so that $\mathrm{Proj.map}\ \varphi$ is defined, and assume $\varphi$ realises $C$ in the sense of `IsVariableChangeHom`: it fixes the classes of all constants $a\in T$, sends the class of $X_0$ to that of $u^2X_0+rX_2$, the class of $X_1$ to that of $u^3X_1+u^2sX_0+tX_2$, and the class of $X_2$ to that of $X_2$. Assume finally that the morphism $\mathrm{projModelCR}\,(W.\mathrm{toProjective})\to\mathrm{projModelCR}\,(W.\mathrm{toProjective})$ obtained by transporting along the equality of schemes coming from $C\bullet W=W$ and then applying $\mathrm{Proj.map}\ \varphi$ is the identity. Then $C=1$, that is $u=1$ and $r=s=t=0$.
--
--   This is the rigidity statement underlying the identification of automorphisms of a Weierstrass projective model with Weierstrass variable changes: a change of variables whose induced morphism of projective models is the identity must be trivial. It is used by [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.exists_variableChange_map_fstHom_eq_one_and_smul_eq_of_iso_of_projMap_comp_eq`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.exists_variableChange_map_fstHom_eq_one_and_smul_eq_of_iso_of_projMap_comp_eq) to pin down the variable change attached to an isomorphism of models.
